    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "A non-empty, closed, convex subset K ⊂ H is called a cone, if R+K ⊂ K and K (−K) = {0} hold. A cone K is called generating if any x ∈ H can be written as x = x+ − x− for some x± ∈ K. In a Hilbert space any generating cone is nonﬂat, that is there exists a constant aK > 0, independent on x, such that in the representation x = x+ −x− the vectors x± can be chosen so that"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 151.079, 552.396, 298.877, 571.57 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "x± ≤ aK x . (4)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 11,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 54.0, 510.636, 298.89, 553.329 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The set K∗ = {f ∈ L(H ;R) : f(K) ⊂ R+} ⊂ H ∗ = H is called adjoint cone. If K is generating, then K∗ is normal, i.e., there is a constant bK > 0 such that x ∈ K, y−x ∈ K imply"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 53.999, 494.148, 298.782, 517.449 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "x ≤ bK y . A cone K is called selfadjoint if K∗ = K. In a Hilbert space any selfadjoint cone is normal [13]."
  }, {
    "type" : "list",
    "pdfua_tag" : "L",
    "id" : 13,
    "level" : "3",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 53.631, 386.988, 299.102, 491.414 ],
    "numbering style" : "arabic numbers",
    "number of list items" : 2,
    "list items" : [ {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 53.999, 439.116, 298.902, 491.414 ],
      "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal",
      "font size" : 10.101,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Deﬁnition 1: Let K be a generating and selfadjoint cone in H . System (1) is called Wazewski [14] with respect to K (also called monotone [15]) if its evolution operator Ω satisﬁes Ω(t,s)K ⊂ K for all t ≥ s ≥ τ.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 53.631, 386.988, 299.102, 443.774 ],
      "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal",
      "font size" : 10.101,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Deﬁnition 2: We say that (1) is stable in K if for any ε > 0 and any t0 ≥ τ there is a δ = δ(ε,t0) > 0 such that x0 ∈ Bδ∩K =⇒ x(t;t0,x0) <ε, t ≥t0; if, in addition, the δ can be chosen independent on t0, then (1) is called uniformly stable in K;",
      "kids" : [ ]
    } ]
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 54.0, 327.348, 298.981, 384.254 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "asymptotically stable in K if it is stable in K and there is η = η(t0) > 0 such that x0 ∈ Bη ∩ K =⇒ limt→∞ x(t;t0,x0) = 0; if, in addition, η can be chosen independent on t0, then (1) is called uniformly asymptotically stable in K."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 54.0, 291.948, 298.955, 324.903 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "If any of the above properties holds with H on the place of K, then we drop ”in K” in their deﬁnitions. Let system (1) be decomposed in two subsystems as follows"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
